WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.330 --> 00:00:01.450
- I used be the smartest.

00:00:01.450 --> 00:00:03.440
Made sure I was the
smartest guy in the room.

00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:05.320
Now, if I'm the smartest guy in the room,

00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:06.153
I'm in the wrong room.

00:00:06.153 --> 00:00:06.986
- You're in the wrong room.

00:00:06.986 --> 00:00:08.880
- I believe in this
philosophy of do it now.

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:12.690
99.9 percent of the people
are zeroing themselves out,

00:00:12.690 --> 00:00:15.619
they're doing 28 days a month, not 31.

00:00:15.619 --> 00:00:18.260
(whoosing)

00:00:18.260 --> 00:00:19.320
- Need motivation?

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:21.520
- Watch the top ten with Believe Nation.

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:22.430
- What's up Believe Nation?

00:00:22.430 --> 00:00:24.230
It's Evan, I believe in you,

00:00:24.230 --> 00:00:25.790
and this channel is designed

00:00:25.790 --> 00:00:28.510
to be a part of your
daily success routine,

00:00:28.510 --> 00:00:30.670
so let's get your motivation to a ten

00:00:30.670 --> 00:00:32.630
and get you believing in you.

00:00:32.630 --> 00:00:35.010
Grab a snack and chew on
today's lessons from a man

00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:36.540
who went from starting with nothing

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:39.155
to becoming a millionaire by age 32,

00:00:39.155 --> 00:00:41.000
going broke, losing it all,

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:43.800
and then gaining it all
back again and more.

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:45.030
He's David Meltzer,

00:00:45.030 --> 00:00:48.338
and here's my take on his
top ten rules of success.

00:00:48.338 --> 00:00:50.921
(upbeat music)

00:00:58.220 --> 00:01:00.170
Okay, let's kick it off
with rule number one.

00:01:00.170 --> 00:01:02.240
Shift your energy.

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:04.870
- You can think, and say,
and do certain things,

00:01:04.870 --> 00:01:06.140
and believe certain things,

00:01:06.140 --> 00:01:08.660
but if you carry an energy it's different.

00:01:08.660 --> 00:01:10.810
It doesn't matter what
you're trying to manifest.

00:01:10.810 --> 00:01:11.643
Let me give you an example.

00:01:11.643 --> 00:01:14.270
There's a lot of people
that date the same person

00:01:14.270 --> 00:01:15.640
again, and again, and again,

00:01:15.640 --> 00:01:17.067
or they have the same business problem

00:01:17.067 --> 00:01:19.130
again, and again, and again.

00:01:19.130 --> 00:01:20.260
Same obstacles.

00:01:20.260 --> 00:01:22.347
No matter what they do you seem to,

00:01:22.347 --> 00:01:24.360
"Why, why is this always happening"?

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:25.531
It's cause you carry an energy.

00:01:25.531 --> 00:01:26.364
- I agree with that.

00:01:26.364 --> 00:01:29.010
- So what I analyze, and I went to India

00:01:29.010 --> 00:01:31.860
and kind of learned this stuff
about myself is number one,

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:34.740
my siblings were all
hyper-intelligent students.

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:36.390
They all went to the Ivy Leagues.

00:01:36.390 --> 00:01:37.880
So I kind of had a chip on my shoulder

00:01:37.880 --> 00:01:39.990
that I didn't go to
Harvard, Penn, or Columbia.

00:01:39.990 --> 00:01:41.970
My siblings were much more academic,

00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:44.640
so I had that going, then
when I was little I was hyper,

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:45.690
and they were good students.

00:01:45.690 --> 00:01:47.800
My grandma who, my mom was a teacher,

00:01:47.800 --> 00:01:49.280
would take us after school

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:53.210
was this wise old, kind
of Yoda type of character.

00:01:53.210 --> 00:01:54.600
And, she would always say to me,

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:57.800
I would go, "Grandma, I'm
bored, I don't want to study!"

00:01:57.800 --> 00:02:00.180
She goes, "Only stupid people get bored.

00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:02.430
Smart people think of things to do."

00:02:02.430 --> 00:02:04.770
Well this changed my cellular memory,

00:02:04.770 --> 00:02:08.380
my neuro-pathways, and
into my code, my DNA.

00:02:08.380 --> 00:02:09.740
So my energy shifted.

00:02:09.740 --> 00:02:10.760
What did that mean though?

00:02:10.760 --> 00:02:14.120
That means I projected my
insecurity about being stupid.

00:02:14.120 --> 00:02:16.900
Made me an ego driven guy.

00:02:16.900 --> 00:02:19.740
Who then surrounded himself
with the wrong people,

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:21.680
and I used to be the smartest,

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:23.244
made sure I was the
smartest guy in the room.

00:02:23.244 --> 00:02:25.560
Now, if I'm the smartest guy in the room,

00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:26.393
I'm in the wrong room.

00:02:26.393 --> 00:02:27.226
- You're in the wrong room.

00:02:27.226 --> 00:02:29.230
- Rule number 2, Do it now.

00:02:29.230 --> 00:02:30.400
- The second thing is,

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:32.920
I believe this philosophy of do it now.

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:35.457
Which kind of realms on
this whole congregate like,

00:02:35.457 --> 00:02:37.193
"Hey, can you introduce me right now?"

00:02:37.193 --> 00:02:39.263
Immediately, when
anything's come to my life,

00:02:39.263 --> 00:02:41.630
I ask myself, "Can I do it now?"

00:02:41.630 --> 00:02:42.537
So, "Hey, can you refer this?"

00:02:42.537 --> 00:02:43.760
"Yeah, hold on."

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:44.650
I'll make phone calls.

00:02:44.650 --> 00:02:45.530
You've been in meetings with me.

00:02:45.530 --> 00:02:46.861
It's like almost ADD, but it's not.

00:02:46.861 --> 00:02:50.547
It's just, talk about saving time.

00:02:50.547 --> 00:02:52.310
Anything you can do now,

00:02:52.310 --> 00:02:54.870
you at least saved twice as much time.

00:02:54.870 --> 00:02:56.280
The minute you don't do something now,

00:02:56.280 --> 00:02:59.180
it'll take you minimum
twice as much time to do it.

00:02:59.180 --> 00:03:00.190
Plus you got to remember it,

00:03:00.190 --> 00:03:02.580
plus you can become
statistically unsuccessful,

00:03:02.580 --> 00:03:05.690
exponentially unsuccessful
the longer you wait on it.

00:03:05.690 --> 00:03:07.983
So, I actually have now,
on my Do it Now strategy,

00:03:07.983 --> 00:03:10.840
not only do things now, but have a folder

00:03:10.840 --> 00:03:12.320
which is called Do it Now,

00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:15.740
so it's things I would do
now if I was capable of.

00:03:15.740 --> 00:03:17.150
Something that's that important.

00:03:17.150 --> 00:03:19.550
So, I immediately after I'm doing it now,

00:03:19.550 --> 00:03:22.260
and doing this, I'll go
to my Do it Now folder,

00:03:22.260 --> 00:03:23.393
so I won't forget.

00:03:24.255 --> 00:03:26.520
And those are the important things.

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:28.240
So I have this system of doing it now,

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:29.560
which only saves me time,

00:03:29.560 --> 00:03:31.500
and makes me more
statistically successful.

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:34.430
- Rule number 3, Survive Failure.

00:03:34.430 --> 00:03:36.126
You're story to me, really is one of

00:03:36.126 --> 00:03:38.570
being able to rebuild,

00:03:38.570 --> 00:03:41.260
and so few people, A, can do it,

00:03:41.260 --> 00:03:42.740
and, B, the one's that can and have

00:03:42.740 --> 00:03:44.330
don't want to talk about it.

00:03:44.330 --> 00:03:46.300
So, how do you think about failure?

00:03:46.300 --> 00:03:47.950
How have you conceptualized in your mind,

00:03:47.950 --> 00:03:50.320
why are you able to
talk so openly about it?

00:03:50.320 --> 00:03:53.630
- You know, I did an
interview with Ryan Leaf,

00:03:53.630 --> 00:03:55.240
and we were talking about big failures,

00:03:55.240 --> 00:03:57.559
and his failure was even
more public than mine.

00:03:57.559 --> 00:04:01.096
But, the number one shameful
thing of losing everything,

00:04:01.096 --> 00:04:04.387
and the most courageous thing
was to face our mothers.

00:04:04.387 --> 00:04:05.460
- That's interesting.

00:04:05.460 --> 00:04:07.180
- You know, you talk about the public,

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:09.950
and I said today, I had
Sheriffs line up at my

00:04:09.950 --> 00:04:11.960
Rancho Santa Fe home, and moving trucks

00:04:11.960 --> 00:04:13.110
to take everything out.

00:04:14.065 --> 00:04:17.040
33 homes alone in San Diego, gone.

00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:18.630
Golf courses, Ski Mountain,

00:04:18.630 --> 00:04:20.940
so beyond my community, and associates,

00:04:20.940 --> 00:04:23.570
and all of this, and I was
already working for Lee.

00:04:23.570 --> 00:04:25.280
This is from past transgressions.

00:04:25.280 --> 00:04:28.382
I was already on my path
and journey of fulfillment,

00:04:28.382 --> 00:04:31.800
but the hardest thing was to
walk through my mom's house,

00:04:31.800 --> 00:04:34.740
and, I get choked up,
and I had to tell her

00:04:35.700 --> 00:04:40.700
not only did I fail myself,
but I felt I failed her.

00:04:41.110 --> 00:04:42.640
It was really, really tough.

00:04:42.640 --> 00:04:47.377
So, that failure, to me,
was the toughest part.

00:04:47.377 --> 00:04:50.010
So, for me, all the other things

00:04:50.010 --> 00:04:51.710
were just learning experiences,

00:04:51.710 --> 00:04:54.174
but I had to get over the shame of that.

00:04:54.174 --> 00:04:56.920
Here, they took my mom's house.

00:04:56.920 --> 00:04:58.390
My dream of getting rich

00:04:58.390 --> 00:05:00.838
was only to buy my mom a house and a car.

00:05:00.838 --> 00:05:02.290
You know, I grew up with nothing.

00:05:02.290 --> 00:05:05.410
Six kids, single mom, so for me,

00:05:05.410 --> 00:05:08.300
to make it back, I was
already on that journey,

00:05:08.300 --> 00:05:11.972
and I felt as if I could
stay in a place of giving

00:05:11.972 --> 00:05:15.170
and faith, and I mean faith in myself,

00:05:15.170 --> 00:05:17.850
and faith in the universe,
faith in others of service,

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:20.400
that everything would come
back to me, and it did.

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:24.100
- Rule number four, Don't
take anyone's advise.

00:05:24.100 --> 00:05:25.350
- You went to Tulane Law School.

00:05:25.350 --> 00:05:26.183
- Yes, Sir.

00:05:26.183 --> 00:05:27.016
- And you graduate there,

00:05:27.016 --> 00:05:28.600
and within nine months tell
them what happened to you.

00:05:28.600 --> 00:05:31.360
Cause I want you all to
hear the ups and downs

00:05:31.360 --> 00:05:33.210
of real life business, and real life

00:05:33.210 --> 00:05:35.440
from one of the most successful
people in the country.

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:36.273
So, what happens at law school?

00:05:36.273 --> 00:05:39.420
- So, I was out of law school,
I have two choices for jobs.

00:05:39.420 --> 00:05:40.700
And it's the recession.

00:05:40.700 --> 00:05:42.360
One was to be a real lawyer.

00:05:42.360 --> 00:05:43.679
Oil and Gas Litigator.

00:05:43.679 --> 00:05:44.930
You know, big money.

00:05:44.930 --> 00:05:47.460
All I want to do is be rich,
it's why I went to law school.

00:05:47.460 --> 00:05:49.860
And then the second was
to work in the internet.

00:05:49.860 --> 00:05:54.020
And, I got offered a job to
sell legal research online,

00:05:54.020 --> 00:05:55.430
by West Publishing.

00:05:55.430 --> 00:05:57.050
Big, big legal publisher.

00:05:57.050 --> 00:05:59.010
And so I go to my mom, cause
you'll appreciate this.

00:05:59.010 --> 00:06:00.990
I go to my mom, "Hey
what should I do mom?"

00:06:00.990 --> 00:06:01.950
My big advisor, you know,

00:06:01.950 --> 00:06:03.910
I grew up with a single mom, six kids,

00:06:03.910 --> 00:06:05.817
and she, without blinking, is like

00:06:05.817 --> 00:06:07.620
"You need to be a real lawyer

00:06:07.620 --> 00:06:10.112
cause this internet thing is a fad."

00:06:10.112 --> 00:06:11.950
So she calls the internet a fad,

00:06:11.950 --> 00:06:14.263
and I always say, cause
I like to teach lessons,

00:06:14.263 --> 00:06:18.280
biggest lesson of my life was
just because somebody love you

00:06:18.280 --> 00:06:20.330
doesn't mean they give you good advise.

00:06:20.330 --> 00:06:24.700
And, I see so many people,
entrepreneurs, in relationships,

00:06:24.700 --> 00:06:26.930
they ask for advise for people
that don't know anything.

00:06:26.930 --> 00:06:28.640
My mom's a second grade teacher.

00:06:28.640 --> 00:06:29.473
What does she know about technology.

00:06:29.473 --> 00:06:31.274
- Beautiful sole, but
not a technology expert.

00:06:31.274 --> 00:06:33.910
- No, and if I would have followed,

00:06:33.910 --> 00:06:35.740
it would've I think slowed down,

00:06:35.740 --> 00:06:39.170
or at least not allowed me to
have the acceleration I had.

00:06:39.170 --> 00:06:40.986
So, I took the technology job.

00:06:40.986 --> 00:06:45.680
Single, money hungry, in a
sales job in the internet.

00:06:45.680 --> 00:06:46.640
- So, be very careful,

00:06:46.640 --> 00:06:48.350
just because you love
them or they love you,

00:06:48.350 --> 00:06:50.779
of thinking they have
some expertise in an area

00:06:50.779 --> 00:06:52.600
that you don't.

00:06:52.600 --> 00:06:53.433
They probably don't.

00:06:53.433 --> 00:06:55.830
So often times we take
advise from the wrong person.

00:06:55.830 --> 00:06:57.330
Derails our dream, so that's lesson one.

00:06:57.330 --> 00:06:58.420
- One more thing too.

00:06:58.420 --> 00:07:00.560
We end up resenting them which is worse,

00:07:00.560 --> 00:07:02.560
so all the people we love the most,

00:07:02.560 --> 00:07:05.470
we end up resenting them
because they gave us bad advise.

00:07:05.470 --> 00:07:06.970
And meanwhile, we should be accountable

00:07:06.970 --> 00:07:08.460
because we asked the second grade teacher

00:07:08.460 --> 00:07:09.480
for internet advise.

00:07:09.480 --> 00:07:11.660
That's the worst part.

00:07:11.660 --> 00:07:14.440
- Rule number five, Practice gratitude.

00:07:14.440 --> 00:07:17.050
- I tell people today, "If
you want to change your life,

00:07:17.050 --> 00:07:19.090
it's as easy as two simple words.

00:07:19.090 --> 00:07:20.580
Thank you."

00:07:20.580 --> 00:07:22.770
In fact, the best habit that you can have,

00:07:22.770 --> 00:07:24.640
I've done research for the last ten years,

00:07:24.640 --> 00:07:26.850
in quantum physics, meta physics, physics,

00:07:26.850 --> 00:07:28.930
and I will tell you the
best effective habit

00:07:28.930 --> 00:07:33.010
that you can have is to say
thank you before you go to bed,

00:07:33.010 --> 00:07:35.160
and when you wake up.

00:07:35.160 --> 00:07:38.450
If you can say or think thank
you before you go to bed,

00:07:38.450 --> 00:07:40.580
and say it and think it when you wake up,

00:07:40.580 --> 00:07:41.820
for 30 straight days,

00:07:41.820 --> 00:07:44.830
I guarantee you it'll change your life.

00:07:44.830 --> 00:07:47.840
How many here think you can
do that for 30 straight days?

00:07:47.840 --> 00:07:50.093
Invariably, everybody raises their hand.

00:07:51.400 --> 00:07:53.400
The saddest part is by tonight,

00:07:53.400 --> 00:07:56.427
half of you will not
say or think thank you.

00:07:56.427 --> 00:07:59.400
By the morning, another half of you

00:07:59.400 --> 00:08:01.500
will not say or think thank you.

00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:04.520
And unfortunately, in three
days, almost all of us

00:08:04.520 --> 00:08:06.410
will forget to say thank you.

00:08:06.410 --> 00:08:09.860
I've given you the easiest way, gratitude,

00:08:09.860 --> 00:08:11.250
to change your life,

00:08:11.250 --> 00:08:13.730
and yet we're so far in our own way,

00:08:13.730 --> 00:08:16.630
we can't even say thank
you for 30 straight days.

00:08:16.630 --> 00:08:19.130
- Rule number six, Ask big.

00:08:19.130 --> 00:08:22.150
- You might as well do as
many good deeds as you can.

00:08:22.150 --> 00:08:24.440
Open as many doors,
smile at as many people,

00:08:24.440 --> 00:08:26.170
hug as many people as you can,

00:08:26.170 --> 00:08:30.553
and then when you create void
of giving in service, ask big.

00:08:31.540 --> 00:08:34.470
In this human vibration,
this pragmatic world,

00:08:34.470 --> 00:08:37.780
ask big, ask for it all
cause it will come to you.

00:08:37.780 --> 00:08:40.320
And that's, I think,
something I did subconsciously

00:08:40.320 --> 00:08:42.170
when I was 25 right out of law school.

00:08:42.170 --> 00:08:44.420
And it's something I do
consciously, subconsciously,

00:08:44.420 --> 00:08:45.770
and unconsciously now.

00:08:45.770 --> 00:08:48.773
I ask to empower 75,000 people.

00:08:48.773 --> 00:08:52.340
I want to change the world
to make people happy.

00:08:52.340 --> 00:08:54.140
- And who are you asking that of?

00:08:54.140 --> 00:08:55.110
- The universe.

00:08:55.110 --> 00:08:58.050
So, whatever you believe
in, whatever you believe in,

00:08:58.050 --> 00:09:00.810
I don't care if it's God,
Jesus, Mohammad, Joseph Smith,

00:09:00.810 --> 00:09:02.930
the 12th man if you're a Sea Hawks fan.

00:09:02.930 --> 00:09:05.250
I don't care, but ask.

00:09:05.250 --> 00:09:07.410
Ask the universe, ask who you think.

00:09:07.410 --> 00:09:08.630
Put it out there.

00:09:08.630 --> 00:09:09.830
You know, there's three ways.

00:09:09.830 --> 00:09:11.410
You got what you think, say, and do.

00:09:11.410 --> 00:09:12.730
That's one way to put it out there.

00:09:12.730 --> 00:09:15.100
Subconsciously, the
neuro-pathways in your mind.

00:09:15.100 --> 00:09:16.850
40,000 of the same thoughts.

00:09:16.850 --> 00:09:17.790
Put it out there.

00:09:17.790 --> 00:09:19.510
And then finally, your energy.

00:09:19.510 --> 00:09:21.484
Your DNA, your fingerprint on life.

00:09:21.484 --> 00:09:23.890
That's what truly puts it out there,

00:09:23.890 --> 00:09:26.050
and that system of
conscious, to subconscious,

00:09:26.050 --> 00:09:28.620
to unconscious is what allows you

00:09:28.620 --> 00:09:32.180
to truly attract rapidly and
accurately what you want.

00:09:32.180 --> 00:09:35.090
- Rule number seven, Provide value.

00:09:35.090 --> 00:09:36.650
- We're goal oriented people.

00:09:36.650 --> 00:09:37.483
- Yes.

00:09:37.483 --> 00:09:40.040
- We played sports where
it's all about winning,

00:09:40.040 --> 00:09:41.917
and so what I used to do is I'd attach,

00:09:41.917 --> 00:09:43.833
"once I graduate high
school I'll be happy,

00:09:43.833 --> 00:09:45.755
I get a scholarship to
college, I graduate."

00:09:45.755 --> 00:09:47.980
All this, and every time it occurred

00:09:47.980 --> 00:09:50.200
I still was in the same state of mind.

00:09:50.200 --> 00:09:53.030
What I learned to do was
to attach the happiness,

00:09:53.030 --> 00:09:55.040
this bliss from the outcome.

00:09:55.040 --> 00:09:57.623
Now the difference is
most people get concerned,

00:09:57.623 --> 00:10:00.090
"How can you be motivated
without an outcome?"

00:10:00.090 --> 00:10:01.010
No, no, no.

00:10:01.010 --> 00:10:03.090
I have outcomes, and I pray every morning.

00:10:03.090 --> 00:10:04.830
This is a truly abundant thing.

00:10:04.830 --> 00:10:06.337
My first prayer every morning is,

00:10:06.337 --> 00:10:09.263
"My God put in front of me
ten people that I can help."

00:10:09.263 --> 00:10:11.310
- That you can help, that you can help.

00:10:11.310 --> 00:10:13.760
- That I can help, and I've
shifted the paradigm of value

00:10:13.760 --> 00:10:15.950
understanding outcomes and happiness.

00:10:15.950 --> 00:10:18.415
So, I used to, and maybe
you'll understand this.

00:10:18.415 --> 00:10:20.020
I'm a great salesman.

00:10:20.020 --> 00:10:20.853
- You are.

00:10:20.853 --> 00:10:22.950
- I can oversell, backend
sell, and lie to you.

00:10:22.950 --> 00:10:23.783
I can cheat you.

00:10:23.783 --> 00:10:25.650
I've done it when I was in my 20's.

00:10:25.650 --> 00:10:28.230
I would shade the truth, you know.

00:10:28.230 --> 00:10:31.790
I sold stuff, and it
didn't make me feel good.

00:10:31.790 --> 00:10:33.610
What happened was, I created a void

00:10:33.610 --> 00:10:34.650
for me to fill all the time.

00:10:34.650 --> 00:10:36.996
I'd make you promises, and
I'd live on this premise,

00:10:36.996 --> 00:10:39.810
"I'm going to exceed
everybody's expectations."

00:10:39.810 --> 00:10:41.294
That's my goal, right.

00:10:41.294 --> 00:10:44.036
First of all, talk about bullshit

00:10:44.036 --> 00:10:48.170
How many times have you actually
seen, in a business deal,

00:10:48.170 --> 00:10:49.970
exceeded the other parties expectations.

00:10:49.970 --> 00:10:50.803
Very rarely.

00:10:50.803 --> 00:10:51.636
- Very rarely.

00:10:51.636 --> 00:10:52.700
Especially if you've
set those expectations

00:10:52.700 --> 00:10:53.533
artificially high.

00:10:53.533 --> 00:10:54.390
- Which I did.

00:10:54.390 --> 00:10:56.010
- The way you exceed
is by not setting them.

00:10:56.010 --> 00:10:58.189
- Right, by not charging or selling,

00:10:58.189 --> 00:10:59.437
and that's what I started doing.

00:10:59.437 --> 00:11:02.400
But, what was cool was, I
started with this prayer,

00:11:02.400 --> 00:11:05.400
and then I said, "What if I
started the day with this energy

00:11:05.400 --> 00:11:07.390
that God put a whole bag

00:11:07.390 --> 00:11:09.230
of hundred dollar bills in front of me,

00:11:09.230 --> 00:11:10.499
and my job all day long

00:11:10.499 --> 00:11:13.040
was to trade hundred
dollar bills for twenty."

00:11:13.040 --> 00:11:15.450
So, whatever I did, I was
going to provide value.

00:11:15.450 --> 00:11:17.940
As a father, as a husband,
as business partner,

00:11:17.940 --> 00:11:19.522
as a partner, as a philanthropist.

00:11:19.522 --> 00:11:23.187
You'll see I ask everyone
either unconditionally

00:11:23.187 --> 00:11:24.764
"How can I be of service?"

00:11:24.764 --> 00:11:25.597
- You do.

00:11:25.597 --> 00:11:26.430
You said it me the first time we spoke.

00:11:26.430 --> 00:11:27.800
- How can I be of service, I mean it.

00:11:27.800 --> 00:11:29.160
- Yeah, I know you do.

00:11:29.160 --> 00:11:30.981
- I know that that's my biggest blessing.

00:11:30.981 --> 00:11:32.580
I'm not lazy.

00:11:32.580 --> 00:11:34.010
I wake up at four a.m.

00:11:34.010 --> 00:11:35.968
I work really hard for others,

00:11:35.968 --> 00:11:38.120
but I also, when I work hard for others,

00:11:38.120 --> 00:11:41.180
I have my intention, my
focus on what I want.

00:11:41.180 --> 00:11:44.610
- Rule number eight,
Focus on being the best.

00:11:44.610 --> 00:11:46.800
- Let's say that you want to be

00:11:46.800 --> 00:11:48.540
the best fitness trainer in the world.

00:11:48.540 --> 00:11:50.410
I don't know if that's reality,

00:11:50.410 --> 00:11:52.080
but let's just say you
want to be that trainer.

00:11:52.080 --> 00:11:54.440
Okay, would you like to be
the best trainer in the world,

00:11:54.440 --> 00:11:55.890
and make a shit load of money,

00:11:55.890 --> 00:11:57.359
or just be the best trainer?

00:11:57.359 --> 00:11:58.800
- First option.

00:11:58.800 --> 00:12:03.652
- Yeah, the money comes so it's not about,

00:12:03.652 --> 00:12:05.410
what's not about the money.

00:12:05.410 --> 00:12:06.523
That's not my end goal.

00:12:06.523 --> 00:12:08.345
I don't attach the money as my goal,

00:12:08.345 --> 00:12:11.300
I attach my consistent, persistent pursuit

00:12:11.300 --> 00:12:13.970
of my potential of being the best trainer.

00:12:13.970 --> 00:12:15.620
I guarantee the best trainer in America

00:12:15.620 --> 00:12:17.143
makes a shit load of money.

00:12:17.143 --> 00:12:20.030
You know, Bill Parsons is
one of my favorite coaches.

00:12:20.030 --> 00:12:23.075
He got into coaching not to make money.

00:12:23.075 --> 00:12:25.250
John Madden, you know who he is?

00:12:25.250 --> 00:12:26.083
- Yes.

00:12:26.083 --> 00:12:27.870
- John Madden got into
coaching not to make money,

00:12:27.870 --> 00:12:30.175
but putting his name on EA Sports,

00:12:30.175 --> 00:12:34.440
on Madden, he makes more
money than anyone else

00:12:34.440 --> 00:12:35.930
for his name.

00:12:35.930 --> 00:12:37.890
But, it's not about the money,

00:12:37.890 --> 00:12:38.990
why does he do it?

00:12:38.990 --> 00:12:41.129
Cause he helps so many
people with that money.

00:12:41.129 --> 00:12:43.800
The universe rewards you.

00:12:43.800 --> 00:12:45.100
Money's just an energy.

00:12:45.100 --> 00:12:47.760
- Rule number nine, Be consistent.

00:12:47.760 --> 00:12:51.270
- There's a consistency that
makes people successful.

00:12:51.270 --> 00:12:53.050
What happens is we lie to ourselves,

00:12:53.050 --> 00:12:55.580
and I'll use health cause
you're and expert at it,

00:12:55.580 --> 00:12:58.610
but I see this in
nutrition and in exercise.

00:12:58.610 --> 00:13:00.077
People will tell me after one month,

00:13:00.077 --> 00:13:02.620
"Gosh, why did I get incremental results

00:13:02.620 --> 00:13:03.640
or no results at all?"

00:13:03.640 --> 00:13:05.794
I said, "Because you zeroed yourself out."

00:13:05.794 --> 00:13:09.180
The kids that showed
up during spring break

00:13:09.180 --> 00:13:10.815
to the event that I had.

00:13:10.815 --> 00:13:12.467
The one's that were there,

00:13:12.467 --> 00:13:14.630
and they had a lot of other distractions,

00:13:14.630 --> 00:13:16.210
they're the ones that don't zero out.

00:13:16.210 --> 00:13:18.048
They're the ones that get the exponential

00:13:18.048 --> 00:13:19.850
power of the universe.

00:13:19.850 --> 00:13:21.835
Meaning, if I do something every day,

00:13:21.835 --> 00:13:23.810
day one I get x to the first,

00:13:23.810 --> 00:13:26.780
day two to the second,
third, third, fourth, fifth.

00:13:26.780 --> 00:13:29.380
Most people, when it comes to nutrition,

00:13:29.380 --> 00:13:33.760
they're always day six
they zero themselves out.

00:13:33.760 --> 00:13:35.510
Then they start over first, second,

00:13:35.510 --> 00:13:37.340
and during a month, they
may zero themself out

00:13:37.340 --> 00:13:38.510
three or four times.

00:13:38.510 --> 00:13:39.630
At the end of the month

00:13:39.630 --> 00:13:41.780
they didn't get the exponential results.

00:13:41.780 --> 00:13:43.530
If you stick to something everyday,

00:13:43.530 --> 00:13:45.790
this idea of being more interested,

00:13:45.790 --> 00:13:47.970
really asking the extra questions,

00:13:47.970 --> 00:13:49.080
going the extra mile,

00:13:49.080 --> 00:13:51.070
which is completely empty in my opinion.

00:13:51.070 --> 00:13:52.597
If you want no competition in your life,

00:13:52.597 --> 00:13:54.313
go the extra mile.

00:13:54.313 --> 00:13:58.100
99.9 percent of the people
are zeroing themselves out,

00:13:58.100 --> 00:14:00.950
they're doing 28 days a month, not 31.

00:14:00.950 --> 00:14:01.810
- And rule number ten,

00:14:01.810 --> 00:14:04.210
the last one before a
very special bonus clip

00:14:04.210 --> 00:14:06.520
is be radically humble.

00:14:06.520 --> 00:14:09.403
What is something you wish
you knew when you were 21?

00:14:10.440 --> 00:14:12.500
- Oh, that's an easy question for me.

00:14:12.500 --> 00:14:13.620
Two words.

00:14:13.620 --> 00:14:16.200
Radical humility.

00:14:16.200 --> 00:14:18.830
I wish somebody would've
taught me the ability

00:14:18.830 --> 00:14:21.210
that I didn't know, and it's
the biggest problem I have

00:14:21.210 --> 00:14:23.940
with my interns and young
associates at my business,

00:14:23.940 --> 00:14:25.750
you don't know what you don't know.

00:14:25.750 --> 00:14:28.500
So, feel good about asking for help.

00:14:28.500 --> 00:14:32.260
Asking for help is giving
a gift to people like me.

00:14:32.260 --> 00:14:34.970
You know, when you ask for
help you become an investment

00:14:34.970 --> 00:14:35.990
of that person.

00:14:35.990 --> 00:14:38.130
And then, don't forget,
like you said earlier,

00:14:38.130 --> 00:14:40.260
just cause you don't have a
lot of money or experience

00:14:40.260 --> 00:14:42.210
doesn't mean you can't help that person.

00:14:42.210 --> 00:14:44.570
So, if someone would've told me, "David,

00:14:44.570 --> 00:14:46.140
be radically humble.

00:14:46.140 --> 00:14:49.891
Ask for help, and then
provide help to others."

00:14:49.891 --> 00:14:53.207
That's my signature teaching tool here is,

00:14:53.207 --> 00:14:55.670
"Hey, ask for help and then follow up

00:14:55.670 --> 00:14:57.520
with what can I do for you."

